BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:surf-artist-in-residence-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261112T145448Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: Sanford Underground Research Facility: Artist-in-Residenc
 e Program 2027 (Lead\, South Dakota)
DESCRIPTION:The SURF Artist-in-Residence program invites artists to create 
 work inspired by the Sanford Underground Research Facility in Lead\, South
  Dakota. At 4\,850 feet deep\, SURF is the deepest underground laboratory 
 in the United States\, housed in the former Homestake Gold Mine\, and host
 s experiments in physics\, biology\, geology and engineering.\n\nOrganisat
 ion: Sanford Underground Research Facility (SURF)\nLocation: Sanford Under
 ground Research Facility\, Lead\, South Dakota\, USA\, in the Black Hills.
  The call does not state a residency or nationality restriction\; travel\,
  housing and per diem for both visits are covered.\nAward: USD 5\,000 stip
 end paid in two installments\, plus up to USD 5\,000 in additional funds t
 he artist may apply for to create the artwork. Transportation (airfare\, r
 ental car or mileage)\, housing and per diem are covered for both visits\;
  a studio space and guided surface and underground tours are provided\; re
 turn shipping of the exhibition is covered up to USD 7\,000.\nDuration: Fo
 ur-week on-site residency in summer 2027 (scheduled between 22 May and 31 
 July in coordination with SURF)\, plus a one-week exhibition installation 
 and guest-lecture visit in October 2027.\n\nMore: https://sanfordlab.org/p
 rograms/SURFAiR?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://sanfordlab.org/programs/SURFAiR?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Sanford Underground Research Facility\, Lead\, South Dakota\, USA\
 , in the Black Hills. The call does not state a residency or nationality r
 estriction\; travel\, housing and per diem for both visits are covered.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:effea-call-5-festival-residencies-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261112T145448Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:Deadline: EFFEA Call #5: European Festivals Fund for Emerging Artis
 ts
DESCRIPTION:The European Festivals Fund for Emerging Artists (EFFEA)\, an i
 nitiative of the European Festivals Association co-funded by the European 
 Union\, opens its fifth call: 50 residencies for 50 emerging artists (indi
 viduals\, groups or collectives) hosted by partnerships of around 150 fest
 ivals\, each led by one leading festival with a minimum of two partner fes
 tivals from different eligible countries.\n\nOrganisation: European Festiv
 als Association (EFA)\nLocation: Residencies hosted by festival partnershi
 ps of at least three festivals from three eligible countries (most of Euro
 pe plus Tunisia and Ukraine). Leading festivals and artists must be based 
 in an eligible country\; festivals from Israel\, Palestine\, Switzerland\,
  Turkey and the UK may join as partner festivals only\, and artists from t
 hose countries may also be proposed. Note: festivals apply\, proposing the
  artists\; artists cannot apply directly.\nAward: 50 residency grants: 40 
 Discovery grants of EUR 8\,000 (for artists at an early career stage) and 
 10 Springboard grants of EUR 15\,000 (for artists established at home and 
 ready to break through internationally). A minimum of 80 percent of the gr
 ant must cover costs incurred by the artists (fees\, travel\, accommodatio
 n\, subsistence). An own contribution of EUR 1\,000 (Discovery) or EUR 2\,
 000 (Springboard) is deducted from the paid grant. No application fee.\nDu
 ration: Residencies implemented between 1 January and 31 December 2027\, c
 o-produced by one leading festival and at least two partner festivals\n\nM
